## Bandit Level 3 → Level 4

**Challenge:**
The password for the next level is stored in a hidden file in the inhere directory.

**Solution:**
bandit3@bandit:~$ pwd
/home/bandit3
bandit3@bandit:~$ ls -a
.  ..  .bash_logout  .bashrc  inhere  .profile
bandit3@bandit:~$ cd inhere
bandit3@bandit:~/inhere$ ls -la
total 12
drwxr-xr-x 2 root    root    4096 Oct 14 09:26 .
drwxr-xr-x 3 root    root    4096 Oct 14 09:26 ..
-rw-r----- 1 bandit4 bandit3   33 Oct 14 09:26 ...Hiding-From-You
bandit3@bandit:~/inhere$ cat ...Hiding-From-You
2WmrDFRmJIq3IPxneAaMGhap0pFhF3NJ


**Explanation:**
First use command pwd to find out what directory you are currently in then use ls command to see what other directories i can change to.
Then use cd to change directory to inhere.
Use ls -a or ls -la to find hidden files.
Use cat command to read file contents and get the password

**Password:**
2WmrDFRmJIq3IPxneAaMGhap0pFhF3NJ

**What I learned:**
Use ls -a to find hidden files and use cd to change working directory.
